>I can't seem to figure out why this alpha can't see
>outside of the local group
>(telnet, ftp, etc returns host not found)

Two things to check:

Is you nameserver working? Try nslookup. Even if it works
you can still have conflicts between NIS and DNS that cause normal apps to
fail. Look at resolv.conf closely. Avoid NIS if at all possible.

Try a netstat -r and make sure that you have valid valid "default" route. You
should see at least 3 routes, one for teh local subnet, one for localhost, and
one for default.

If the default is not there, "route add default gw-addr" should get things
running.

