I had exactly the same problem: how does one start up at boot time a daemon
that wants to run as user "foo"?  I finally opted for an inelegant solution:
start the daemon up in the "/sbin/rc3.d" startup script using the
"rsh nodename -l foo ..." command.  I had to take care to redirect the
(remote) standard output and error streams to the (remote) null pseudodevice,
even though it appeared to me that the daemon startup command produced no
output at all.


