In article <kevin.6.00118C7A@ins.infonet.net>,
Kevin Houle <kevin@ins.infonet.net> wrote:
>Some of our nn users are experiencing strange results with keystrokes in
>other applications after using nn. This is with nn 6.5.0b3 running on an
>alpha osf/1 V2.1 box. Is this a known condition?

I've just patched my  nn.6.4.18's term.c to do termios ioctl
function calls  (HAVE_TERMIO defined) instead of termio calls.
The termio ioctl calls were leaving the noncanonical IO parameters
min and time set incorrectly, which was afflicting emacs and 
other programs expecting the more sane defaults.

If this corrects the problem for you, then you are running into the 
same problem.

alias nn 'nn; stty min 1 time 0'

Of course, programs relying on those values would be wise to set them
as nn does.

-- 
