In article <32tjo2$isg@racerx.mse.jhu.edu>,
I <timmo@RacerX.mse.jhu.edu> wrote:
>Gary Veum <veum@boa.gsfc.nasa.gov> wrote:
>>While running Enhanced Security on a OSF/1 v2.0 machine with xdm configured
>>correctly, I'm trying to have an NCD attach to it.  I get the error on the
>>NCD "Cannot Obtain Database Information on this Terminal".
>
>Gary:
>
>You need to add a line for your Xserver to /etc/auth/system/devassign.  If
>the Xserver is bobo.gsfc.nasa.gov, the line might look like this:
>
>	bobo.gsfc.nasa.gov\:0|bobo.gsfc.nasa.gov\:0.0: \
>		v_devs=bobo\:0,bobo\:0.0 \
>		v_type=xdisplay:chkent:
>
>You might need to add the full name to the v_devs= entry.
>
>Also, you may also be able to specify wildcards on some of these entries.

Also, Gary corrected an omission on my part.  The /etc/auth/system/ttys
database also needs an entry.  That entry would look something like this:

bobo.gsfc.nasa.gov\:0|bobo.gsfc.nasa.gov\:0.0: \
	t_devname=bobo.gsfc.nasa.gov\:0: \
        t_xdisplay:t_login_timeout#0:chkent:

Like the devassign entry above, it can probably be replaced by a wildcard
entry.  Apologies for forgetting this in the first place.

