My Saturday was occupied by dicking around with replacement disks
for my DEC Alpha 3000-300LX, since the RZ26L crapped out (2 months
old).  Since I couldn't wait for the warranty replacement, and since
the RZ26L (as most of you know) is about as noisy as a blender on the
"fine puree" setting, I decided to use something else.

First I went to the computer store.  I found a 2.1Gb Seagate ST12550N
on sale for $1399 and bought it (take what you can get on a Saturday).
The Alpha would not recognize the Seagate under any circumstances --
just ignored it completely.  Drive light blinked when probing with
"show dev" but it just didn't jive with the DEC.  I stuck it in a Sun
(which recognized it immediately) and took the Sun's disk.

The 1.2Gb Toshiba MK538-FB from the Sun worked wonderfully in the
Alpha, even as the primary boot disk.

Anyway, I haven't seen anyone collecting /etc/disktab entries for
third-party disks that are known to work (actually I *have* seen
the Ultrix disktabs file on gatekeeper, but it's clearly way out of
date and is furthermore not comprehensive enough to be useful).  Since
I'm assuming plenty of people want to have the option of using a
