The DEC 2100 "Sable" is a real good bet as a server.  It's an upgradable
SMP machine.  At $29K, you're getting one CPU, but it goes to four in
the current lineup.  Those processors are 190 MHz today, and expected
to go to 275 MHz in October 1994.  This gives you pretty good in-place
scalability.  Processors also are not that expensive--about $9K each
last I checked.  The others are essentially headless workstations, and
are not nearly as upgradable.  The 2100 also has much better peripheral
expansion, via its PCI and EISA slots.  Unless you're real sure you
won't need more CPU horsepower in the future, the 2100 is the way
to go.  

jse


