Unfortunately, it *can't* be replaced with a wildcard, not even in T3.0.
This is rather frustrating for us since we have at our site potentially
4500 hosts that may want X connections. Furthermore, you also can't
have SysV LAT ttys or SysV ptys as wildcards either (/dev/lat/n and
/dev/pts/n). Since we need a few hundred of the former and over five
hundred of the latter, we're going to be having rather large devassign
and ttys files when our sable goes into full service in a few weeks' time.

Our QAR to DEC about this has been downgraded into "Customer requests
that wildcarding mechanism be supported in these databases."

