In article <skoogCv1vo7.58L@netcom.com>, Jim Skoog <skoog@netcom.com> wrote:
>What capabilities and utilities are provided with AdvFS without
>adding the layered AdvFS utilites on DEC OSF/1?  

Basically, not having the utilities renders advfs useless.  For example,
you can only create an advfs partition on 1 disk, you can't have multiple
disks, because you need addvol for that, and that only runs with the
utility license.  You also won't have the defragment utility and a
few other things.

I'll never understand it.  Even IBM got this one right with AIX.  DEC
comes out with something even better, then braindeads their magnificent
feat of engineering with something as stupid as requiring more $$$'s to
make advfs work on multiple disks.  Makes me wonder why I keep buying 
the stuff sometimes.

BTW, has anybody made /usr under OSF an advfs?  I don't think there's
any reason not to, but I'm not sure I've thought of everything yet.
