Why don't you just build all your kernels with every rz and tz slot in place to start off with? Saves much hassle, doesn't waste significant space :-) Also you don't need to be in single user mode or even on the same machine (as long as it's the right version of the right OS on the right architecture) to rebuild a kernel. I reckon it's my responsibility to take the machines down for the minimum time possible, and I wouldn't be too popular if adding a new disk to a file server involved this procedure. I've shutdown, connected a new disk, and rebooted sufficiently quickly that no-one actually noticed before now!

