gallatin@isds.duke.edu (Andrew Gallatin) writes:

>Speaking of AdvFS, does anybody know if any sort of remote-dumping
>capability is planned?  There doesn't seem to be a vrdump & vrrestore,
>which is quite annoying..

>Has anybody had success with piping a vdump through an rsh and into the
>raw tape device on a remote machine?

We are dumping /usr and home directories from advfs to a remote tape drive
by piping rsh through dd to write the drive, with the dump script running
on the tape drive host:

rsh alpha "/sbin/vdump -0 -f -" | dd bs=100b of=/dev/tape/no-rewind

Works just fine so far.  If you're tight on tape space, you can even put
a compress or gzip in the pipeline (or use the vdump compress option).

