I see two "odd" things, niether of which may be significant.

1) You are specifying backup parameters for the systems. Is thi really
something you want to do? I usually mount nfs volumes 0 0.

2) Can you get away with mounting a forieign system from a relative mount
point? Shouldn't it be /u@saturn?

And, as a side issue, do you want to have nfs file systems in fstab which are
hard mounded and not backgrounded? I always use rw,bg,soft for nfs. Soft may be
inappropriate in your case, but I think bg is a real good idea. Else you won't
be able to boot unless sparc and saturn are both available.


And, finally and least important, I always use the FQDN for all systems in case
DNS is not set up to tack on the local domain name. If not that, put them in
you /etc/hosts (yuck!).

