I can't help with disktab entries - but I've successfully added 2 different
Seagate drives to Alphas running OSF/1 v1.3. They were a 2Gb ST42400N and
a 9Gb ST410800N.  This method was given to me by DEC CSC for any third party 
disk for which I didn't have a disktab description - (I have only tried it on
these models plus a loaned 3Gb Seagate drive) :

- boot genvmunix and single user,  mount -a
- rebuild the kernel with the relevant SCSI Id and reboot with new kernel.
-make newfs - For non-standard geometry do
   disklabel -w -r rz{n} /dev/rrz{n}c
This reads the disk's actual geometry and writes it to the headers, -
- which can now be edited:
   disklabel -e /dev/rrz{n}c

This saved me a large amount of guesswork in getting the correct disktab -
especially as I was swapping in and out with loan and trial disks at the time!


