"Mainstream" depends a lot on your viewpoint.  If you can provide a little
more information on the application or platform that you want to transfer
the files to, I can check to see if it's something we can accommodate.

The audio files are Microsoft .WAV files which are playable on any machine
running Windows or Windows NT and on many Unix systems as well.  I think
that there are .WAV players for the Macintoshs too, but I'm not 100% sure.
There's a public domain package called SOX which will do all kinds of
conversions on these files, from changing wrapper formats to changing 
audio sample rates.

The movie files are in Microsoft .AVI (Audio/Video Interleaved) and the
video frames are compressed with the Motion JPEG codec.  This algorithm
typically requires hardware assist for playback on PCs, so it isn't as 
widely used as some of the software playback algorithms, but there are
vendors like VideoLogics who produce PC accellerator boards for Motion
JPEG which will play these files back under Windows 3.1 with Video for
Windows installed.

Send me the details on what format you are trying to get to and I'll see what 
I can do.

