The kernel includes support for the built-in audio device on the DEC 3000
workstations, but you need to install some higher level software to actually
make it do anything useful.

A product called Multimedia Services for OSF/1 includes support for the
built-in audio as well as the Sound & Motion J300 audio & video option.  It
provides you with a server to manage the device, client libraries for 
accessing it, and a set of applets to get you started.  There's an audio
recorder/editor/player with a Motif U/I that works well as a Mosaic audio
'viewer.'  If you want sources for an audio player, you can install the
Developer's subset as well as the Run-Time and look in /usr/examples/mme.

The license for Multimedia Services is bundled with all the DEC 2000 & 3000
Alpha workstations that run DEC OSF/1 and the actual kits can be found on
the Layered Products CD.

