I built emacs 19.25 last week on a 2100 with OSF.  You need the emacs patch
from gatekeeper of course.  I didn't have GNU make and used the make that was
provided with the OS.  I got the error at line 269 in the make file just like
you did.  However, the Digital consultant who was with me (who said he didn't
know much about UNIX) suggested that we just comment out the TAGS section
of the Makefile.  This worked perfectly (surprised me) and emacs 19.25 
built OK after that.  I think the TAGS section is for the etags and ctags
programs and I didn't want to use them.  You could probably make them manually
by examining the Makefile.  Anyways it ran without any problems under 
X-Windows/Motif.  



