Pradeep Balachandran <pradeep@phzeus.phys.lsu.edu> wrote:
>
>
>I am having a problem with NFS mounting discs between an Ultrix machine
>and an Alpha.  I NFS mounted a disc resident on the ultrix machine on 
>to a Dec-Alpha running osf/1 v2.0.  A user on the alpha is not able
>to write into his area on the disc.  I maintain seperate password data
>bases on the two machines.  I tried playing with the gid and uid and 
>made it identical in both the passwd files but still it would not let me
>write onto the disc.  I can't figure out a way around this problem.  I 
>export the file system with -r=0 option which allows the root on the 
>alpha to be able to write on to the nfs mounted disc but restricts the 
>other users.
>
>Any help would be appreciated.
>
>Thanx
> 
>

First, if you specified -r=0 then it will do what you said, and only let root
on the alpha write (i.e. no one else can). The other thing that you need to 
do is set the permissions on the ultrix machine to let "others" write (anyone
not logged into the ultrix machine is an "other", including root on the alpha).

I think that should work.

l8r,

