Ajay Shekhar <ashekhar@luciferencore.com> wrote:
>What I don't know, is if there is a group of terminals that can be
>designated as "secure" so that a "root login" can be dome from them. In
>essence, if you have more than one console then you may be able to login
>as root from only those consoles.

For OSF/1 the secure ttys are listed in /etc/securettys (or
/etc/auth/system/ttys in a trusted system).

Normally this list includes '/dev/console', 'local:0' and ':0' which
means that you can login as root using X (it would be a bit hard login
in as root on a workstation without accounts otherwise)

