In article <32avib$qoa@mack.rt66.com> wombat@aquilagroup.com writes:
>
>I have an OSF2.0 system configured with /tmp as an mfs. When
>I attempt to dump a filesystem, dump dies:
>
># dump 0f /dev/null /usr/local/src                            
>dump: SIGSEGV received -- ABORTING!
>Abort process
>
>Any info on this? Is there a bug fix, or am I just doing
>something stupid? 8^{)>
>

Fixed in V3.0. The problem is the line in /etc/fstab that starts
With the size description, i.e.:

	-s32000 /tmp    mfs    rw 1 0

In order for dump to work, you have to comment out that line. The
fact of whether a MFS actually is mounted is irrelevant, so one
can either mount /tmp in a init script instead of through fstab
or do a temporary edit during dumps. Yuck.

