>In article <32dh7p$44o@mozo.cc.purdue.edu>, cjdc@staff.cc.purdue.edu (Chris Christian) writes:
>If you do want to access the subset anyway, do the following (assuming the DEC
>OSF/1 CDROM is mounted on /mnt):
>
>cd / 
>uncompress < /mnt/ALPHA/BASE/OSFBASE200 | tar xpf - ./usr/bin/passwd

This doesn't work, since ./usr/bin/passwd is a (hard) link to
./usr/bin/chfn (it fails with the message 'can't link ...')

Using Gnu Tar it's possibel to extract it using:

tar xpzf /mnt/ALPHA/BASE/OSFBASE200 ./usr/bin/passwd ./usr/bin/chfn

It's posssibel to extract using the standard tar by adding
./usr/bin/chfn at the end of your command, but the Gnu Tar solution is
much nicer :-)


