Josanne Otway (otway@bnr.ca) wrote:
: Has anyone ported HPUX or SUNOS applications to OSF1? I would
: like to know if it is straight forward to do ports or if there
: are a lot of differences between OSF1 and regular unix. 

OSF1 is regular Unix. 

But, as you say, Unix != Unix.   And portabilty will vary depending
on the APIs, options, commands, etc. you use.  But the good news for
OSF1 is that it's a pretty good port target.  Probably better for 
SunOS (which is BSD-flavored) than HP-UX (which is SVR2/3 flavored).
Interestingly, you may have an easier time getting from SunOS to OSF1 
than to Solaris (which is SVR4-flavored).   

But a real answer requires knowing about your app.  If it uses a
proprietary enhancement such as Sun's pixmap lib, or HP's VUE or
clustering, say,  it's going to be much harder than if it is a plain 
or standards-conformant app.


