I decided to install bison-1.22 before making gcc-2.6.0:
(in my bison-1.22 directory)
/configure
make
su root
make install

gcc-2.6.0 compiled in under 2 hours without fail on my DEC7000-610 (although it
indeed works, I did get 'char 5 line 1' differences using the compare command
in the installation docs).

I simply did the following:

configure --target=alpha-dec-osf
make LANGUAGES=c
make bootstrap LANGUAGES=c BOOT_CFLAGS="-g -O"
for file in *.o ; do cmp $file stage2/$file ; done
make install CC="stage2/xgcc -Bstage2/" CFLAGS="-g -O" LANGUAGES=c


