>I am just moving from DECstations to alphas, and in the process discovered
>that I could not set the font in dxmail on either system (dxmail -fn doesn't
>work), except in the folder area with the resource

'-fn foo' on the command line of X Toolkit applications is equivalent to having
something like "*font: foo" in the application resource file. The reason it doesn't
work for dxmail (and others..) is that Motif uses font lists, not simple fonts,
for specifying what font to use. Have a look in /usr/lib/X11/app-defaults/DXMail
for the strings "fontList" and/or "FontList" for hints on how to set fonts.
	-Rick


