>Our Ultrix machine automatically bumps the nice level of jobs from 0 to 4
>after they've been running for 10 minutes.  I would like to get OSF/1 1.3
>to do this (or something similar, like changing the jobs to a nice level
>of 10) on our Alphas, but I'm not sure how I would go about doing this.

There are to ways to achieve this: you can either tell the kernel to do
this; therefore you have to add "options AUTONICE" to your /sys/conf/NAME
file and rebuild the kernel (for more information see the "Guide to
System Administration" chapter 5).

The more flexible way is to use the autonice program you can find on
ftp.mrc-bbc.ox.ac.uk:/pub/dec_alpha/autonice-0.2.tar.gz. The advantages
are that you don't have to rebuild the kernel and that you can change the 
autonice program to behave exactly the way you want.

