>How do I add demons such as httpd to let it start at boot time. In
>Ultrix I add them into rc.local, but I am not sure how I can add them
>to /sbin/rc3.d.

I have installed the following script to /sbin/rc3.d/S97httpd (use the
appropriate number). All files in /sbin/rc3.d are executed while
the system is changing to run level 3, so you can add scripts of your own.
Numbering the files is neccessary to have them executed in the right order.

Ralf.

######################### begin #####################################
#!/sbin/sh
#
# HISTORY
#
# @(#)httpd
#
# Ralf Eckstein 27.7.1994
#

PATH=/sbin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin
export PATH

case "$1" in
'start')
	/usr/sbin/httpd  -r /usr/local/lib/www/httpd.conf
	echo "http daemon started"
	;;
'stop')
	;;
esac
######################### end #######################################
-- 
