   saunders@castor.che.wisc.edu (Brian Saunders) writes:

>I was looking at turning on the logging for our ftp daemon.  Where is ftpd
>called in the startup process, so I could add the appropriate option to
>the line which executes it?  I scanned the appropriate man pages and the
>System Administrator's manual, but didn't see anything helpful.

The ftp daemon is started by inetd when the connection is requested. Look in
/etc/inetd.conf ..

ftp     stream  tcp     nowait  root    /usr/sbin/ftpd          ftpd

in your case, this would be changed to 

ftp     stream  tcp     nowait  root    /usr/sbin/ftpd          ftpd -l


