>1. When I try to post I get all the way to the Send command and then it
>   tells me that inews is not found. What did you guys use?

I fetched the whole nntp 1.5 distribution and used the stuff in the 'inews'
directory in there.  It's a mini-inews (I'm still not sure what it's a
miniature _of_, but that's another story).  The code you need is in that
directory, although it uses a couple of header files from 'common' and
'server', if memory serves.

>2. How do you get a list of newsgroups.

Trn comes with a program called "getactive" that is just a nice front-end
for a LIST command sent to your news server.  Try it -- but pipe it through
a pager or into a file, as the output can be quite long (depending on how
many groups your server carries).

>3. How do you see a directory of articles in a news group.

From within trn you can use "+" to toggle the thread selector on and off.
If you're in thread selector mode, you'll see the articles (by definition
of 'selector mode').  Otherwise, you can use the '=' command to list the
articles in the older, sequential format that rn users should be more
familiar with.

Hope this helps.

