|>Is there anyway I can pull a fresh 
|>copy of gettydefs out of the subsets on the CD, while running standalone?

Two ways come to mind.  First, check in /etc for a file called
".proto..gettydefs".   Copying that into gettydefs should get you
up and running.  If you can't find this file, then try the following:

	Boot the system to single user.

	Mount the distribution cd.

	Mount /usr.

	Now do the following:

		cd /
		/usr/bin/zcat </cdrom/ALPHA/BASE/OSFBASE200 | \
			tar xvpf - ./etc/gettydefs


						Frank

		


