In article <31tcit$46r@unicorn.ccc.nottingham.ac.uk>, pdxjfp@evol.nott.ac.uk (John F Peden) writes:
|>Hi
|>
|>Could someone shed any light on how to activate the /proc file system.

|>I RTFM ( man 4 proc ) and it said to manually mount it with a 
|>
|>mount -t procfs  /proc /proc
|>
|>but this only results in a device busy error.
|>
|>
|>Any suggestions ??

Make sure that no processes are in the /proc directory when you do the
mount.  That is, don't have /proc as your current directory.

If you want to mount /proc at boot time, add the following line to
/etc/fstab:

/proc   /proc   procfs rw 0 0

Hope this helps.

					Frank


