NNTP-Posting-Host: fman.zko.dec.com

Consider that a library might contain more than one possible
block data initialization subprogram - initializing the SAME
common block to different values...  There is no way to select
which block data subprogram to load, EXCEPT by specifying the
name in an external statement.  This is the reason that none
of the block data initialization routines are selected unless
there is an external reference to resolve from the main routine,
the name of the particular block data routine desired!

Dave Eklund


