In article <2usj1n$gjo@adam.spu.edu>, francais@adam.spu.edu (Olivier T
CALLE) writes:

ADVFS V1.3 and V2.0 have a bug that will cause News systems to
appear to run out of disk space.  The bug has to do with how ADVFS
handles deleted file fragments (most News files are file fragments since
they are typically smaller than 8K).  This disk space is not really lost,
however, it is only available for allocation as file fragments.  Normally
this would not be problem except that the statfs() system call does
not return free file fragment space so the News system will eventually
think that the system is out of free space (when most of the free space
is accounted for by free file fragments).

The bug is fixed in the field test version of V3.0.

Hope that helps.



